here we will learn about the how size shrinks while going larger screen to smaller screem 

lets understand how grid will work with tailwind css to build web pages for mobile or smaller screeen

lets breakdown the project 
this is the main section of the screen
<div class="m-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-12">
What this means:
m-4 → margin all sides
grid → enable CSS grid
gap-4 → spacing between items
sm:grid-cols-12 → 12 column layout ONLY on small screens and above
how tailwind works 
default → mobile
sm → tablet
md → laptop
lg → desktop

👉 “How does Tailwind handle responsiveness?”

 answer: Tailwind uses a mobile-first approach where base styles apply to smaller screens, and breakpoint prefixes like sm, md, lg override styles for larger screens using min-width media queries.